  "voting_summary": "Rhode Island pairs 20 days of early in-person voting (33% of the 2024 vote) with no-excuse mail (10%), and mail must arrive by the 8 p.m. Eastern close. Pre-processed mail and early votes are released first, then election day precincts report, and the state is essentially complete the same night, with a small federal-ballot pool (overseas voters) reported statewide. Mail ran D+52 and early voting D+18 against D+4 on election day, so the first batches are the bluest of the night.",
